 "notes": "Hexagonal phase-D diffraction interchange record. The crystallographic pattern was imported from Dioptas/JCPDS, while both executable EOS records use the separately printed AntA and AntB ambient volumes in Shieh et al. (2000), Table 2. The atom sites are the composition Mg1.11Si1.89H2.22O6 single-crystal refinement of Yang et al., American Mineralogist 82, 651-654 (1997), doi:10.2138/AM-1997-5-627; its lattice is the one stored here. H is the refined split/disordered site and Mg substitutes at 5.5% on the nominal Si site. Phase D is compositionally variable, and this structure is a representative model rather than an exact refinement of the Fe-bearing AntA/AntB EOS specimens. The legacy peaks are retained.",
